\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\fs24 2rectoa (Prolog:) \plain \f1\i\fs24 Samaritanus ille piissimus spoliatum videns hominem ab Ierusalem in Iericho descendentem tunc in latrones impios incidisse\u8230 \'85\plain \f1\fs24  2rectob (Text:) \plain \f1\i\fs24 Ad primum sic proceditur et arguitur: Quod creatura possit habere authenticam\plain \f1\fs24  (\u252 \'fcbergeschrieben: \plain \f1\i\fs24 actionem\plain \f1\fs24 )\plain \f1\i\fs24  respectu termini creationis\u8230 \'85
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\fs20 -- (Teil-)Ed.: Balic, Bibliotheca Mariana medii aevi, 1931, S. XXVI, Hs. f\u252 \'fcr die Edition beigezogen; Ed.: Ioannis Duns Scoti. Opera omnia (1950ff), Bd. 11,12 (bis IV, d. 30). Lit.: Stegm\u252 \'fcller, RS, Nr. 421; Meier, The manuscripts of Duns Scotus, in Mediaeval and Ren. Stud. 3 (1954).}

